{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/579206-two-dream-park-esque-kickstarters","id":579206,"title":"Two Dream Park-esque Kickstarters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-04T15:57:09-07:00","id":579206,"title":"Two Dream Park-esque Kickstarters","content":"I've recently run across two projects being crowdfunded that might interest people - particularly our fellow forum members based out of Great Britain. They're being promoted as &quot;immersive experiences&quot; . . . but look a lot like LARP, with professional game masters and special effects.<br /> <br /> The first is <b>Hyde </b>( <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/hyde/hyde-0?ref=nav_search\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...ref=nav_search</a> ). Set up by the guys behind the <b>2.8 Hours Later</b> zombie run, <i>Hyde </i>is basically a one shot LARP scenario,. Participants take on the role of human guinea pigs testing the Jekyll Corporations new &quot;superhuman&quot; drug, demonstrating its effectiveness by solving various puzzles in a maze. But then things start to get . . . strange. Some rooms remain locked, no matter how many puzzles you solve. But at the same time, maintenance doors - which are apparently supposed to be locked - start opening, leading out of the maze, and into the ransacked offices of the corporation. As you go along, trying to find a way out, you start running into blood . . .<br /> <br /> <i>Can you escape the maze? <br /> <br /> Will you discover the secret of the Jekyll Corporation? <br /> <br /> Or will Hyde find you first?</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kickstarter</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> <b><u>This is the story</u></b><br /><br />You're taking part in experimental trials of a new drug developed by the Jekyll Corporation. It's designed to modify the capabilities of the human body, giving you the power to control your environment simply by controlling your physical state (your pulse rate, breathing, posture etc).<br /> <br /> Armed with some wearable tech your assignment is to navigate your way though a maze of connected rooms, using your new powers to complete a series of increasingly challenging tasks along the way. <br /> <br /> But this is a smart maze: it knows where you are, and how you\u2019re doing. You begin to realise that someone \u2013 or something \u2013 is working against you. You'll need to stay calm to retain control of your surroundings. Because there's only one way out of this maze, and that's through discovering the true story of Jekyll &amp; Hyde.<br /> <br /> We plan on building <b>Hyde</b> in London and New York City, if we hit our stretch goal. It will open to the public in 2016 as a ticketed experience that lasts 45-60 mins experience<br /> <br /> . . .<br /> <br /> <b><u><b>Experience</b></u></b><br /><br /><b>Hyde</b> is an interior environment, a maze made up of rooms, corridors and halls that are linked by doors. Players can experience the maze either individually (scary) or in a small group. As players progress through <b>Hyde</b> they encounter doors that are locked. In order to progress deeper into <b>Hyde</b> the players must unlock these doors. This is achieved by overcoming challenges. Some of these are familiar from computer games and escape the room experiences: solving puzzles, finding hidden keys and so on. Other challenges are deeply unfamiliar; the players must control their body state to open the doors: may be hold their breath, blow forcefully or lower their heart rates. The objective is to find the centre of the maze and get out within a given time.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T16:10:51-07:00","id":579216,"title":"","content":"<b>Crystal Maze</b>, the second project, is over on Indiegogo ( <a href=\"https://www.indiegogo.com/projects/the-crystal-maze-a-live-immersive-experience#/story\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.indiegogo.com/projects/t...erience#/story</a> ). Based on the British tv show (which was actually reimagined as a mini-Game in the <i>Dream Park</i> sequel, <i>The California Voodoo Game</i>), Crystal Maze sends teams through four distinct areas, to win the right to enter the Crystal Dome:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Indiegogo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the 90's, The Crystal Maze, was one of the UK's favourite television shows. Now we're planning for it to return as a live immersive experience right in the heart of London!<br /> <br /> You'll get to play the maze just as contestants did on the original show - placing you at the centre of the action. What we really want, is for people to live the magic of the hit television programme for themselves.<br /> <br /> We will be lovingly recreating the famous set just as it was on the original show. All four famous zones will be present; Aztec, Medieval, Industrial and Futuristic, not forgetting of course, The Crystal Dome!<br /> <br /> We are delighted to be announcing the return of none other than the legendary Maze Master himself, Richard O'Brien! Richard won't be running around the maze himself, but he will be welcoming guests in time honoured fashion... to find out how, you'll just have to come along and see!<br /> . . .<br /> <br /> [Participants] will compete in teams, guided by their own personal Maze Master. Each contestant will play games that test their intelligence, skill, physical ability and mystery...ness. At the experience's finale, each team will be rewarded for the amount of games they have won by converting crystals into precious time in the Dome.<br /> <br /> You will be invited to form teams of 8. Don\u2019t worry if you are a group of 1 or 2, we'll find you some excellent team mates to tackle the maze with. You can also hook up with your friends even if you pledge individually.<br /> <br /> 4 teams will then enter the maze at once, moving through each zone before regrouping at the end to take on the Dome</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}